   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Urticaria likely • Help to identify and advise to avoid triggers2. • Apply calamine lotion as needed. • If recurrent eye problem, check for allergic conjunctivitis 48. • If recurrent nose problem, check for allergic rhinitis 51. • If recurrent cough or wheeze, exclude asthma 138. • For itch, give chlorphenamine 4mg 6-8 hourly. If known with chronic urticaria, give instead cetirizine 10mg daily. • Advise to return immediately if any symptoms of anaphylaxis3 occur. • If no better after 24 hours, discuss/refer.",
   "bbox": [
    599.5,
    273.0,
    705.2,
    534.0
   ],
   "key": "p84-c6824b07"
  },
  {
   "id": "p84-out-e24",
   "page": 84,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Eczema likely • Eczema is a chronic condition with acute exacerbations. • Advise to avoid triggers such as soap, detergents, heat, fabrics that cause itch, overheating at night. • If low mood, stress or anxiety 98. • Wash with aqueous cream (UEA) instead of soap. • If severe, start at Step 3. • Step 1. Moisturise skin with emulsifying ointment (UE) twice a day and immediately after bathing. • Step 2. If no better after 7 days: apply hydrocortisone 1% cream twice a day for 7 days (apply sparingly to face, avoid eyes). If good response, reduce to once a day for 3 days, then stop. Continue with UEA and UE as above. • Step 3. If poor response to hydrocortisone or severe eczema, apply instead betamethasone 0.1% ointment once a day for 7 days (avoid face, neck, flexures). If good response, reduce use to every second day for a few days, then stop. Continue with UEA and UE as above. • For itch, give chlorphenamine 4mg at night for up to 2 weeks. If no better/severe daytime itch, give instead cetirizine 10mg daily. • If oozing/pus/yellow crusts, treat for infection: give cefalexin 500mg or flucloxacillin 500mg 6 hourly for 5 days. If severe penicillin allergy1, give instead azithromycin 500mg daily for 3 days. • Refer if: no better after 2 weeks, extensive involvement or painful pustules.",
   "bbox": [
    365.7,
    263.0,
    582.8,
    534.0
   ],
   "key": "p84-5041ed38"
  },
  {
